WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.050
-Finish him! *dramatic music* When Daniel San hit that crane kick we learned to never give up.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.130
When Lloyd Doppler lifted his boom box we learned love is patient

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:18.540
And when Johnnie and Baby danced we learned how to come out of our shells

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.650
There's something magical about the movies we watched in our youth

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.940
those moments that helped shape our budding personalities

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:26.680
Like when Ferris Bueller taught us 

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.130
-You can never go too far.  Jack Burton taught us... -It's all in the reflexes.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:37.120
And the Ghostbusters taught us  -when someone asks you if you're a god you say yes

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:38.860
As we get older though

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.600
This magic fades.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:49.300
Dampened by our age, experience, and cynicism these days we bring so much with us into the theater it's a miracle we enjoy anything at all. 

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:56.650
But we can have that sense of wonder again. And the answer isn't in bigger special effects, sequels, or reboots.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:01.290
In in characters we care about doing things that excite or inspire us

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.220
Like when Luke learns who his father is.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.350
When Elliott learns how to say goodbye

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.860
And Dee learns to never get on the freeway

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:15.400
The answer is also in us. Let's make movies magic again. Let's turn off our phones and our cynicism.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.880
Let's ignore reviews, hype, gossip, and snark

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:24.680
And just enjoy the show, like when we were younger and George McFly taught us how to stand up for ourselves. 

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.810
The Goonies taught us to never say die. 

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:33.190
And PeeWee taught us there's no basement at the Alamo. -There's no basement at the Alamo. *laughs*

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:44.400
Movies can still teach us a lot about ourselves. We just have to be willing to learn. -Come back tomorrow

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:55.030
*Dramatic Music*

